Provide APIs to get raw submittable extrinsics (without submitting) in order to allow for easier batching.

This allows consumers of the lib to better construct and submit a collection of extrinsics/transactions.

-----
Example:
A vault could disable issuing, and add more collateral in one batch.
```
// disable issuing for vault with DOT collateral
const disableIssuing = vaultsApi.buildAcceptNewIssuesExtrinsic(Polkadot, false);
// we want to add 42 DOT
const collateralAmount = newMonetaryAmount(42, Polkadot, true);
// create extrinsic to add collateral
const addCollateral = vaultsApi.buildDepositCollateralExtrinsic(collateralAmount);
// create batch extrinsic (treat extrinsics atomically - all or none succeed)
const batchExtrinsic = transactionAPI.buildBatchExtrinsic([disableIssuing, addCollateral], true);
// submit batch, and wait for Promise to resolve/reject
await transactionAPI.sendLogged(batchExtrinsic);
```

A bunch of changes collected when developing the repo for simulating the bar of charge:
* refactored code handling histograms of beam populations, such that histogramming and plotting are clearly separated;
* adding a trapezoidal fit to measured beam distributions!
* some new functions to sample and manipulate beam populations - very basic operations, for the time being;

### Proxy mode for SM:
* proxy mode for SM was implemented (removed logic has already implemented in sm-client);
* workers number was increased (by default 4 for docker 2 for helm);
* workers number can be overrode with special env;

### Some fixes
* status code for bad request was changed to 400;
* tracking disable mode in sm-client polling function was added (it resolves waiting procedure finishing for mntc command);

